# Build and distribution artifacts - regenerated by `python -m build`.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Tool caches.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local virtualenvs.
.venv/
venv/

# Throwaway verification venvs and scratch scripts (`python -m venv .check/wheel`, fresh-install runs).
.check/

# The arXiv corpora the acceptance tests audit. They are evidence, not our source: they are rebuilt
# from pinned digests by `scripts/fetch_acceptance_inputs.py`, and a vendored copy would ship
# someone else's paper bytes inside our release.
phase0/sources/
phase3/acceptance-inputs/

# The fetch script's download cache (a 2.2 MB tarball per e-print). Scratch, always re-fetchable.
**/.dl/

# The §15 human-onboarding kit. Regenerated by `python scripts/build_onboarding_kit.py` because it
# contains staged build artifacts, which do not belong in version control.
release/onboarding-kit/

# The TabM working clone Experiment Doctor captured its run provenance from. The capture
# (`phase3/tabm/ed-captured/`) is the evidence; the clone is 174 MB of upstream repository.
phase3/.ed-workdir/

# The Dataset Doctor fingerprint's 48,842 per-row hashes (13 MB). Same principle as the corpora above:
# it is regenerable bulk evidence, not our source, and it is pinned by digest in two places that ARE
# committed - `phase3/tabm/end_to_end_chain.json` (`dd_ref.fingerprint_sha256`) and
# `phase3/tabm/dd/README.md`, which also records the command that rebuilds it byte-for-byte.
phase3/tabm/dd/fingerprint.json

# The Phase 3 brief, kept verbatim as the author's instruction record. Not published: it quotes the
# title of one of the author's own unpublished submissions (the exclusion named in
# `phase2/PAPER_DOCTOR_PHASE2_REPORT.md` section 18), and it is an instruction document rather than a
# deliverable. Its content is reproduced, with that one name withheld, throughout the Phase 3 report
# and `release/RC_AUDIT.md`.
phase3/PHASE3_BRIEF.md
